# Written by mcpp/glib/build.mcpp on every build: glibconfig.h, config.h,
# glib/gversionmacros.h, the three *-visibility.h headers and
# gobject/glib-enumtypes.{h,c}. Nothing in here is checked in.
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS SO THE DIRECTORY DOES. mcpp builds the compiler command line
# from `include_dirs` BEFORE running the build program, and silently drops an
# entry that does not exist yet — so on the first build of a fresh clone the
# generated config.h would be written correctly and then ignored, with glib's
# sources reading some dependency's config.h instead.
